Same fix:

```bash
pip3 install --user "ninja>=1.12"
hash -r
ninja --version
```

Should report 1.12 or higher. If it still shows the old 1.10, the system one at `/usr/bin/ninja` is winning. Check with `which ninja`. If it points at `/usr/bin/ninja`, your PATH ordering is off, so re-run:

```bash
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
hash -r
which ninja
```

Then rebuild:

```bash
rm -rf ~/work/ascend/AscendNPU-IR/build-ubuntu
cd ~/work/ascend/AscendNPU-IR
bash build-tools/build.sh -o build-ubuntu -j 32
```

Verify both tools before starting so you don't discover a third version problem an hour in:

```bash
cmake --version && ninja --version && gcc --version
```
